gedBy","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Who created a client registration (D5, T21.4). The discriminator that separates a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"registration an administrator made from one that arrived over an open endpoint. Three things","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"read it and each would otherwise have to infer provenance from something that is not","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"provenance: * ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"axiam_oauth2::fapi"},{"type":"text","text":" refuses a FAPI profile on anything but"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"Self::Admin"},{"text":" (I5) — a client nobody vetted cannot be financial-grade; * the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"authorization endpoint forces a consent hop for every other value (D4) — an unrelated party"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"gets a question put to the end user, whatever scopes it asked for; * the T21.4 sweeper","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"deletes only "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"Self::Dcr"},{"type":"text","text":" rows, so an administrator’s client is never swept however"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"long it sits unused. "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","overridingTitle":"Admin","identifier":"Self::Admin","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"code":"Admin","type":"codeVoice"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the serde default and therefore what every"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"row written before T21.4 decodes to, which is the truth: they were all created through "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"POST \/oauth2-clients"},{"type":"text","text":" by somebody holding "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"oauth2_clients:create"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol"},"Self::Dcr":{"type":"link","url":"Self::Dcr","title":"Dcr